        <task id="0" uid="fadf7445d4574d2885a5a1ae2434dc36" name="Proposal" meeting="false" start="2026-09-08" duration="14" complete="70" expand="true">
            <notes><![CDATA[Proposal is mostly done, just need to formalize writing and do the Gantt chart]]></notes>
            <depend id="1" type="2" difference="0" hardness="Strong"/>
        </task>
        <task id="1" uid="34e2cd6f09104fb6951b16ebcd1d8d5c" name="Prototype- Vertical Slice" meeting="false" start="2026-09-22" duration="37" complete="0" expand="true">
            <notes><![CDATA[The prototype should be a nearly completed tutorial level. This means that most of the remaining work when we are done is finishing the remaining levels, adding new races of enemies that mostly use the existing subclasses, polishing UI and art stuff. Polishing the gameplay and NPC behaviors is important too.

This means we need:
- A start menu and pause menu (okay if they're ugly)
- Other UI elements (rough, should convey the information and have correct layouts)
- A settings menu for sound and maybe controls (can be ugly)
- The scene where gameplay takes place
- Entities for the captain, crew members of all classes, NPCs of all classes
- Objectives that the enemies target and a way for them to progress towards it
- The player's commanding abilities and UI, and a way for crew members to fight back against the enemies
- Scripted events that trigger for win/loss conditions
]]></notes>
            <task id="9" uid="be445beca32f4b6ab7e67c163c078f24" name="Deliverable for demo submission" meeting="false" start="2026-10-14" duration="15" complete="0" expand="true"/>
            <task id="2" uid="f408a62f5b0447ad80e0af408d1ac164" name="Assets for world environment" color="#ff33ff" meeting="false" start="2026-09-22" duration="8" complete="0" expand="true">
                <depend id="3" type="2" difference="0" hardness="Strong"/>
            </task>
            <task id="3" uid="9e73c43b0f1346078f6e6d15c809b9c8" name="Create world scene" color="#33ff33" meeting="false" start="2026-09-30" duration="15" complete="0" expand="true">
                <notes><![CDATA[This is the level that the game is played in, including but not limited to:
- The ship and its objectives
- Textures for the skybox
- Whatever is needed for the ocean water
- Foliage like rocks, islands, etc. that pop out of water]]></notes>
            </task>
            <task id="4" uid="1b0a81c01df74823860ab0df1c9b0b97" name="NPC classes and capabilities" color="#ffff66" meeting="false" start="2026-09-22" duration="8" complete="0" expand="true">
                <notes><![CDATA[What jobs can NPCs have?
- Allies: e.g. repairs, medics, ranged fighters, melee fighters
- Enemies: e.g. ranged fighters, melee fighters, elite/tanky enemies

Where can enemy/ally NPCs go to or be assigned to?
- Allies: cannons, defend objectives, fight enemies, etc
- Enemies: destroy defenses, fight allies, capture objectives

What abilities do these jobs have? Do certain jobs handle certain assignments better?

]]></notes>
                <depend id="6" type="1" difference="0" hardness="Strong"/>
                <depend id="7" type="2" difference="0" hardness="Strong"/>
            </task>
            <task id="7" uid="171958dcfaff4f5db09d99215c2a320f" name="Assets for interactives and characters" color="#ff33ff" meeting="false" start="2026-09-30" duration="15" complete="0" expand="true">
                <notes><![CDATA[- Objectives on the ship
- Cannons and other defenses
- Characters: The captain, ally and enemy NPCs for each class, for now we only need pirate NPCs. 

it would be best if we could find an asset pack or make models that have the same visual style and match the world scene, and if we can reuse the models to create a variety of subclasses

the parrot and other stuff maybe?
]]></notes>
                <depend id="8" type="2" difference="0" hardness="Strong"/>
            </task>
